   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<span><div><span>Hi,</span></div><div><span></span></div><div><span>I tried running trajectory analysis:</span></div><div><span>trajectory.analysis(f1=shape ~ chkpnt, traj.pts=3, data=gdf, iter=999, print.progress=T)</span></div><div><span><br></span></div><div><span>...after finishing sums of squares calculateion, I got this error:</span></div><div><span><br></span></div><div><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Error in La.svd(center.scale(x)$coords, 0, 1) : \r\n  infinite or missing values in &#39;x&#39;</span></pre></div><div><br></div><div>Since I removed one level of checkpoint, and levels(gdf$chkpnt) still gave the extra level, I tried fixing it with:</div><div><br></div><div>gdf$chkpnt = factor(gdf$chkpnt)</div><div><br></div><div>so the number of levels is now correct (and fits traj.pts), but now I get a different error while running the trajectory analysis (after calculation of sums of squares):</div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;line-height:15px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Error in dimnames(x) &lt;- dn : \r\n  length of &#39;dimnames&#39; [2] not equal to array extent</span></span></pre></div><div><br></div><div>\r\n<span><div><span>length(gdf$chkpnt)</span></div><div><span>[1] 191</span></div><div><span>dim(gdf$shape)</span></div><div><span>[1]  72   2 191</span></div></span>\r\n\r\n</div><div><br></div><div>Does anyone know how can I fix this?<br></div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div><br></div><div>Avi</div></span>\r\n\r\n</div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
